
# GENERATED prepare entry points -- one authored generator, not dozens of committed derivatives.
# Gym's `prepare_script:` contract takes a path and calls a zero-arg prepare(), so every shard or
# task slice needs its own importable module, and those modules differ by a single line. Comitting
# them meant a reviewer could not distinguish a deliberate edit from a stale copy, and they rot the
# moment a shard count changes. The pattern is deliberately broad so a new slice is ignored by
# default; `git add -f` if you ever do want one tracked. prepare.py itself does not match.
prepare_*.py

# GENERATED override yamls -- emitted alongside their prepare scripts, plus the per-experiment
# behaviour arms. Gym composes overrides by PATH, so each variant needs its own file and those
# files differ only in an index or a single knob. Generating them together also makes it
# impossible for a slice's yaml and its prepare script to drift apart.
*_override.yaml

# Local task wiring: helpers that read datasets from a private path and therefore cannot work on
# another machine. Shipping a config that silently points at an unreadable directory is worse
# than not shipping it.
*_common.py
*_shard.py

# Per-launch arm configs generated by the launch scripts (tool surface / search mode / cache).
# Operational, run-scoped, and must live on a shared filesystem so the compute node can read them.
.generated/

# The smoke-slice generator. Validation scaffolding, not the environment: nothing tracked
# references it, and a minimal PR ships the benchmark rather than our way of rehearsing it.
make_shard_scripts.py
